  "description": "THE POST-FAILED-VALIDATION OUT-OF-RANGE SUBSCRIPT, and the hardest parity point in this package. Option 99 is rejected by app/cbl/COMEN01C.cbl:128, line 133 paints the invalid-option message, and PERFORM SEND-MENU-SCREEN RETURNS - so control falls through to line 136, where the filter is NOT guarded by IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON and subscripts CDEMO-MENU-OPT-USRTYPE(99) on a table declared OCCURS 12. COBOL compiled without SSRANGE computes an offset and reads whatever bytes are there; Java would throw IndexOutOfBoundsException, which is a crash the COBOL does not produce and therefore itself a parity violation. The read must be bounded to 1..12 and yield nothing, leaving the filter false, exactly one paint, and the invalid-option message on the screen rather than the No access one.",
